course: dictionary
lesson: 52
title: Accurate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accurate means correct and exact, with no mistakes. An accurate answer is the right answer, and an accurate measurement is one you can trust. «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer under the tail, because it gives an accurate reading.» The reading is correct, so the vet can trust it.
explain: Accurate can also mean hitting the target. An accurate throw, shot or kick lands exactly where you aim. An accurate story is true to the facts, with nothing made up.
explain: In maths and science, you can say how accurate an answer is. A length might be «accurate to the nearest centimetre», which means it is right to the closest whole centimetre. An estimate is quick, but it is less accurate than a careful measurement.
fact: Accurate means correct and exact, with no mistakes.
fact: The forms are accurate, more accurate and most accurate.
fact: An accurate measurement is one you can trust, because the ruler, scale or thermometer was read carefully.
fact: Estimates are quick, but they are less accurate than careful measuring.
fact: Useful phrases: «accurate measurement», «accurate information», and «accurate to the nearest…».
exercise: «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer under the tail, because it gives an accurate reading.» What does accurate mean here? | Ruined | Loud and clear | *Correct and exact | Quick and rough
exercise: Which is more accurate: a quick guess or a careful measurement? | Both are exactly the same | Neither can be checked | *A careful measurement | A quick guess
exercise: An accurate kick hits exactly what you aim at. Which kick is accurate? | Kicking wildly at the sky | Kicking the ball away without looking | Kicking the ball high over the fence | *Kicking the ball straight into the goal you aimed at
test: A step counter counts 30 shakes, but 4 were just bumps. What is the accurate number of steps? | 4 | 30 | 34 | *26
test: Ava's school report lists only checked, true facts. Which phrase describes it? | Curt replies | Glum mood | *Accurate information | Barely a whisper
exam: Which measurement is most accurate? | *Measured carefully with a ruler to the nearest millimetre | Measured to the nearest metre | Guessed by eye
